{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b> Fifth instance </b><br> הזמיר. [Like זמיר עריצים (Isaiah 25:5), meaning as it sounds.] Birdsong:" "התור. From שתי תורים (two turtledoves):" "<b> Third instance </b><br> הנצנים. Moses and Aaron:" "ועת הזמיר. That they sang at the Sea:" "וקול התור. That they entered the Land of Israel:"], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The bracketed text appears to be a gloss explaining that הזמיר here means song in the sense of Isaiah's usage; Ibn Ezra then gives his own reading as birdsong."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:44:03.297642805Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}